---
source: crates/cli/tests/it/help.rs
expression: long_help(path)
---
Trust the devlanes CA and set up hostnames for this machine; asks once.

Works out what this machine needs and lists each step as ok, todo or skip:
  ca        trust the CA in the stores tls.trust names (mkcert's CA with tls.ca: mkcert)
  hosts     install the /etc/hosts helper (macOS and Linux) when *.localhost does not
            resolve to loopback, the user config asks for the hosts file, or the
            daemon needs it for a project
  resolver  send hostnames.tld to the devlanes DNS server (a resolver file, or an
            NRPT rule on Windows) when hostnames.resolver is resolver

Then it asks once before doing the todo steps; sudo asks for your password at
most once. Without a terminal, pass --yes.

Usage: devlanes setup [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --check
          Only report each step; exit 0 when nothing is missing, 1 otherwise

      --remove
          Undo everything: the resolver file or NRPT rule, the /etc/hosts helper and the CA trust

      --keep-ca
          With --remove, keep the CA trusted

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --json
          Print JSON: one document, or NDJSON for streams (same as --output json)

      --output <MODE>
          Output mode [default: agent when an AI agent runs devlanes, plain in CI or without a terminal, else human]

          Possible values:
          - human: Colors and symbols, for a terminal
          - plain: The same information without color, one line per event
          - agent: Terse lines for AI agents: failures first, with next commands, size-capped
          - json:  The daemon's data as JSON, or NDJSON for streams

  -p, --project <PROJECT>
          Use this project instead of the one containing the current directory [env: DEVLANES_PROJECT]

      --file <FILE>
          Use this project file instead of the nearest devlanes.yaml (for example devlanes.prod.yaml); after the first use, -p <name> finds its project

      --lane <LANE>
          Use this lane ([project@]lane, such as 2, feat/checkout or acme@2) instead of the current worktree's

      --yes
          Confirm actions that would ask first; needed when no terminal can prompt

      --quiet
          Print nothing on success; errors still go to stderr

      --env <KEY=VALUE>
          Set a variable for started processes (start, restart, run TASK, exec, lane new --start); repeatable

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Limit waits and streams, such as 30s, 5m or 1h [default for start and wait: 180s]

      --budget <BYTES>
          Cap agent-mode output at this many bytes [default: 16384, minimum: 256]

  -v, --verbose...
          Print timestamped diagnostics of the client and daemon to stderr; -vv for more. A bare devlanes -v prints the version [env: DEVLANES_VERBOSE=1|2]

Examples:
  devlanes setup                       set up what is missing, asking once
  devlanes setup --check               exit 1 when something is missing
  devlanes setup --remove --keep-ca    remove the hosts helper and resolver, keep the CA
